 :reserved-name-collision
 {:collides true
  :name "query"
  :cleared-by :rename-in-the-migrated-component
  :detail
  "src/abb_robotics/main.cljc declares a public `query`, which the pure
   S-expression core reserved as a head on 2026-09-06. The migrated component
   names the same operation store-query. The oracle is unchanged -- nothing was
   renamed in the .cljc -- which is the second of the two options
   lang/q9-wave1-tranche-1.edn :reserved-name-collision names, and the same one
   com-aadhaar and com-aave took. Third pilot, same resolution."}

 :what-this-pilot-exercises-that-the-earlier-two-did-not
 "TWO refs on one spec. `:refs {:parentPartId \"Part\" :childPartId \"Part\"}`
  on BOM. In com-aave every spec was `:refs {}` and expand folded over nothing;
  in com-aadhaar five specs carried exactly one ref, and a fold over one is not
  a fold. Here `refs-of` returns a comma-separated list of two pairs and expand
  parses it as a LIST on the production path for the first time.

  It is asserted by execution, not by inspection -- see :executed below."

 :the-trap-this-port-walked-into
 "The oracle-expand selectors were carried over from com-aadhaar asking for
  `{\"expand\":\"identityId\"}`. BOM has no identityId. Left unchanged, every
  selector would have named a field that does not exist, expand would have
  folded over nothing, and all four arms would have returned the unexpanded
  record -- four green assertions measuring an empty fold, in the very port
  whose novelty is that the fold now runs twice. The field names were corrected
  to parentPartId / childPartId and a fifth selector asking for BOTH was added.

  This is the same shape as the reserved-name collision one layer up: the port
  is mechanical enough that the parts which must NOT be mechanical are the ones
  to check."

